.TH shiftpaper-mode 1  shiftpaper 
.SH NAME
shiftpaper\-mode \- Show or change the cursor tracking mode
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBshiftpaper mode\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIMODE\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show or change the cursor tracking mode.
.PP
Pointer mode (the default) uses Wayland\*(Aqs native pointer events. It works on any wlr\-layer\-shell compositor, and the daemon only draws while the cursor is over visible desktop, which saves battery.
.PP
Hyprland mode reads the global cursor position from the Hyprland IPC socket. Parallax remains responsive even when windows cover the desktop, at the cost of being Hyprland\-specific. Note that Hyprland mode lets the daemon observe cursor positions over arbitrary windows, which is a minor privacy consideration.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
[\fIMODE\fR]
Tracking mode to set. Omit to print the current value
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
pointer: Wayland\-native pointer events. Default. Works on any wlr\-layer\-shell compositor; renders only when the cursor is over visible desktop
.IP \(bu 2
hyprland: Hyprland IPC global cursor polling. Hyprland\-only; sees the cursor even when windows cover the desktop
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
shiftpaper mode            Print the current mode
shiftpaper mode hyprland   Follow the cursor over windows too (Hyprland only)
shiftpaper mode pointer    Go back to the default
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
shiftpaper(1)
.PP
The docs: https://github.com/CPritch/shiftpaper/tree/main/docs
